  "measurement_definitions": {
    "valid_forecast_selection": "Read high_level_records with time>2 s, valid interception_prediction, and time strictly before first force-based robot contact if one exists. Forecasts include diagnostic predictions; planning_usable marks reachability entry present (therefore actual active planner accepted the prediction).",
    "actual_first_contact": "Minimum start_time among source summary contacts whose kind is robot. Stage E recorder requires solved normal force>1e-6 N. Episode start_time is physics-step before_time, giving 1 ms timing resolution.",
    "actual_contact_deadline_overestimate_s": "record.time + interception_prediction.time_to_plane_s - actual_first_contact_s; positive means forecast later than actual first contact. This includes dynamics/geometry/current-plane effects, and is available only in contact cases.",
    "snapshot_deadline_overestimate_s": "(pilot_prediction_plane_x - (minimum eligible robot geom world-X support - ball_radius)) / current_ball_world_vx. This isolates plane geometry at the current recorded configuration, using the same constant-Vx timing approximation; it is not a future physical contact prediction.",
    "all_articulation_deadline_overestimate_s": "(all_articulation_root_radius + ball_radius - pilot_front_offset) / current_ball_world_vx. This is the timing difference between representative plane and all-articulation sphere plane at current root under constant current Vx.",
    "reachable_label": "Original pilot reachability boolean, preserved as evidence; not recomputed under revised final tolerance/plane."
  },
  "native_geometry_support_method": {
    "state_reconstruction": "Compile untouched pilot scene_free.xml through MjModel.from_xml_path. At each high-level record, select exact matching full trace qpos/qvel timestamp (assert mismatch<1e-9 s), assign to independent MjData, call mujoco.mj_forward, then read geom_xpos and geom_xmat. No simulations or policies rerun.",
    "box_min_world_x": "geom_xpos_x - dot(abs(geom_xmat row0), geom_size half_extents)",
    "cylinder_min_world_x": "geom_xpos_x - half_length*abs(axis_world_x) - radius*sqrt(1-axis_world_x**2)",
    "mesh_min_world_x": "geom_xpos_x + min(mesh_vert @ geom_xmat row0), using compiled centered/oriented mesh vertices and actual geom transformation; support extrema of original vertices equal convex hull support in this direction.",
    "union_front": "Minimum world-X support across all 20 E-audited eligible official robot collision geoms, then subtract ball radius; intentionally ignores whether that frontmost geom shares the ball height/lateral coordinate.",
    "all_articulation_radius": "For each geom, sum norms of body_pos offsets from free trunk down its ancestor chain + norm(geom_pos) + native geom_rbound; take maximum. Triangle inequality is invariant to arbitrary joint and trunk rotations, so the same bound applies along world X and lateral Y."
  },
  "conclusion": {
    "revision_needed_for_conservative_geometry_claim": true,
    "recommendation": "Use current_base_world_x-0.81 and rerun full protocol. Keep representative-plane diagnostics separate if retained.",
    "observed_pilot_contact_deadline_optimism_max_s": 0.02408050239359305,
    "observed_snapshot_plane_optimism_max_s": 0.09585187499189396,
    "reserves_interpretation": "Startup 1 s, stopping 1 s and 0.09 m distance reserves appear ample compared with observed deadline discrepancy, but those reserves already serve motion response/braking and should not excuse a geometry deadline that is later than possible collision. No pilot blocking success is reclassified solely by this geometry audit."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The -.81 plane bounds instantaneous collision geometry at current base pose, not unknown future base fore-aft drift or external impact motion.",
    "Constant-current-Vx arrival time remains a current-state empirical forecast. Ball deceleration, accelerations, spin and floor bounces require separate handling; unsupported bounces are planner abstentions.",
    "Earliest union-front sphere/shape plane is more conservative than a height/lateral-conditioned collider. Snapshot timing discrepancy therefore exceeds observed actual-contact timing discrepancy.",
    "Actual contact results and matched-absent goal outcomes are the physical verification; geometry/reachability alone cannot promise interception, blocking, or balance recovery.",
    "This audit preserves pilot labels and outcomes; final rerun uses the revised plane and tolerance and must have separately recorded results."
  ],
